207
00:12:44,122 --> 00:12:45,212
API-001 · 1.

208
00:12:45,212 --> 00:12:48,482
Saving twice: an output named after a native event

209
00:12:49,607 --> 00:12:52,957
(click) on <ui-button> subscribes to both the component's click output

210
00:12:52,957 --> 00:12:56,308
and the native click DOM event on the host element.

211
00:12:56,308 --> 00:12:59,659
The inner <button>'s native click bubbles up to the host,

212
00:12:59,659 --> 00:13:03,680
so save() runs once for the bubbled DOM event and once for

213
00:13:03,680 --> 00:13:04,351
the output.

214
00:13:05,726 --> 00:13:06,882
API-001 · 1.

215
00:13:06,882 --> 00:13:10,352
Saving twice: an output named after a native event

216
00:13:11,477 --> 00:13:15,794
It gets worse: a click on any part of the host outside the inner

217
00:13:15,794 --> 00:13:20,111
button (padding, a gap) fires the native event even when the button is disabled.

218
00:13:21,486 --> 00:13:22,634
API-001 · 1.

219
00:13:22,634 --> 00:13:26,078
Saving twice: an output named after a native event

220
00:13:27,203 --> 00:13:30,535
Fix: never name an output after a native DOM event.

221
00:13:30,535 --> 00:13:34,532
Here the output is not needed at all: native click events from

222
00:13:34,532 --> 00:13:37,197
the inner <button> already bubble to the host,

223
00:13:37,197 --> 00:13:40,195
and a disabled <button> does not dispatch click events,

224
00:13:40,195 --> 00:13:42,193
so (click) on <ui-button> just works.

225
00:13:42,193 --> 00:13:46,190
If a custom event is needed, give it a distinct name (pressed).

226
00:13:47,566 --> 00:13:51,646
API-001 · 2. disabled with no value is falsy

227
00:13:52,771 --> 00:13:55,384
For a static attribute with no value,

228
00:13:55,384 --> 00:13:58,371
Angular passes the empty string '' to the

229
00:13:58,371 --> 00:13:58,744
input.

230
00:13:58,744 --> 00:14:02,104
'' is falsy, so [disabled]="disabled()" leaves the button enabled.

231
00:14:02,104 --> 00:14:06,957
Applications with strict template checking get a compile error instead (a string is

232
00:14:06,957 --> 00:14:11,811
not a boolean), which is better, but HTML-style boolean attributes should simply work.

233
00:14:13,186 --> 00:14:18,003
API-001 · 2. disabled with no value is falsy

234
00:14:19,128 --> 00:14:22,741
Fix: input(false, { transform: booleanAttribute }), which maps '',

235
00:14:22,741 --> 00:14:25,953
'true' and true to true, and 'false', false,

236
00:14:25,953 --> 00:14:29,968
null and undefined to false. numberAttribute does the same for

237
00:14:29,968 --> 00:14:30,771
numeric inputs.

238
00:14:32,146 --> 00:14:36,846
API-001 · 3. kind accepts any string

239
00:14:37,971 --> 00:14:39,381
input('primary') infers string.

240
00:14:39,381 --> 00:14:44,551
"primay" compiles, produces the class ui-button--primay, and renders an unstyled button.

241
00:14:45,926 --> 00:14:49,301
API-001 · 3. kind accepts any string

242
00:14:50,426 --> 00:14:55,151
Fix: a union type, exported so consumers can use it in their own code:

243
