530
00:33:30,171 --> 00:33:33,194
API-003 · Redesigned API

531
00:33:34,319 --> 00:33:37,676
Every request is now satisfied without a library change: the

532
00:33:37,676 --> 00:33:40,026
consumer picks the heading level, the link,

533
00:33:40,026 --> 00:33:42,377
the badge count and the action controls,

534
00:33:42,377 --> 00:33:44,056
and writes the alt text.

535
00:33:45,431 --> 00:33:48,596
API-003 · Redesigned API

536
00:33:49,721 --> 00:33:53,589
The marker directives are more than selectors: they apply the styling

537
00:33:53,589 --> 00:33:56,051
class, they appear in autocomplete and documentation,

538
00:33:56,051 --> 00:33:59,920
and the card can query them (as hasHeader does) to avoid

539
00:33:59,920 --> 00:34:00,976
rendering empty wrappers.

540
00:34:02,351 --> 00:34:05,300
API-003 · Trade-offs to state

541
00:34:06,425 --> 00:34:07,579
Less enforced consistency.

542
00:34:07,579 --> 00:34:10,657
Consumers can now put anything in a region.

543
00:34:10,657 --> 00:34:13,350
Mitigate with marker directives, good documentation examples,

544
00:34:13,350 --> 00:34:16,428
and visual review, rather than by taking control

545
00:34:16,428 --> 00:34:16,812
back.

546
00:34:16,812 --> 00:34:22,199
Projection rules. select matches only elements written directly inside <ui-card> in the consumer's template.

547
00:34:22,199 --> 00:34:26,046
Content wrapped in another element or an <ng-container> needs ngProjectAs.

548
00:34:26,046 --> 00:34:29,124
Projected content is always created by the parent,

549
00:34:29,124 --> 00:34:32,587
even inside an @if in the card (see A11Y-002).

550
00:34:32,587 --> 00:34:34,895
Not everything should be a slot.

551
00:34:34,895 --> 00:34:38,358
Values the card must interpret (for example an elevation

552
00:34:38,358 --> 00:34:41,435
that maps to tokens) stay as typed inputs.

553
00:34:42,811 --> 00:34:44,695
API-003 · Migration

554
00:34:45,820 --> 00:34:47,441
Removing seven inputs is breaking.

555
00:34:47,441 --> 00:34:51,981
Ship the slot API in a minor release and keep the old inputs working

556
00:34:51,981 --> 00:34:56,520
(the template can render the legacy markup when title() is set and project otherwise).

557
00:34:56,520 --> 00:35:00,087
Mark the inputs @deprecated with a pointer to the slot equivalent,

558
00:35:00,087 --> 00:35:03,006
provide an ng update schematic for the simple cases,

559
00:35:03,006 --> 00:35:05,276
and remove them in the next major.

560
00:35:06,651 --> 00:35:09,136
API-003 · Follow-up 1

561
00:35:10,261 --> 00:35:13,551
When would you still choose a configuration (data-driven)

562
00:35:13,551 --> 00:35:16,842
API, for example for a data table's columns?

563
00:35:22,172 --> 00:35:26,075
Choose data configuration for uniform repeated structures where a schema is

564
00:35:26,075 --> 00:35:29,979
useful, such as column identifiers, sorting rules, widths, and value accessors.

565
00:35:29,979 --> 00:35:33,528
Use templates or projection for rich content that varies structurally.

566
00:35:33,528 --> 00:35:37,077
A table can combine typed column metadata with cell templates.

567
00:35:37,077 --> 00:35:41,690
The decision depends on whether consumers need to describe data or compose UI.

568
00:35:41,690 --> 00:35:46,658
Keep the configuration type narrow and avoid callbacks for every possible piece of markup.

569
00:35:48,034 --> 00:35:50,472
API-003 · Follow-up 2

570
00:35:51,597 --> 00:35:54,790
How would you make the entire card clickable while

571
00:35:54,790 --> 00:35:57,629
keeping the title link and action buttons accessible?

572
00:36:03,038 --> 00:36:07,912
Use a real title link as the primary navigation action and separate action buttons.

573
00:36:07,912 --> 00:36:11,046
A stretched-link technique can enlarge the title link's hit

574
00:36:11,046 --> 00:36:13,831
area while carefully preserving interactive controls above it.

575
00:36:13,831 --> 00:36:17,661
Avoid nesting buttons or links inside another interactive element and avoid

576
00:36:17,661 --> 00:36:21,491
a container click handler that hijacks text selection or child actions.

577
00:36:21,491 --> 00:36:24,973
Show clear focus and hover states and test keyboard traversal.

578
00:36:24,973 --> 00:36:29,499
In some cards, keeping only the title clickable is the simplest accessible design.

579
00:36:30,875 --> 00:36:33,664
API-003 · Follow-up 3

580
00:36:34,789 --> 00:36:39,863
How do you document slots so consumers discover them in their editor?

581
00:36:45,091 --> 00:36:48,782
Export named slot directives with clear selectors and JSDoc,

582
00:36:48,782 --> 00:36:52,883
include compile-checked examples, and describe which slots are optional or

583
00:36:52,883 --> 00:36:53,293
repeatable.

584
00:36:53,293 --> 00:36:59,035
Editors can discover directives and their inputs more reliably than an undocumented attribute convention.

585
00:36:59,035 --> 00:37:03,136
Document heading responsibility, image alternatives, empty slots, and layout behavior.

586
00:37:03,136 --> 00:37:08,057
Projection selectors alone do not create typed slot metadata or lazy instantiation.

587
00:37:08,057 --> 00:37:12,979
Use a template contract when the library needs context or deferred creation.

