697
00:44:26,276 --> 00:44:30,127
API-004 · What a strong candidate also mentions

698
00:44:31,252 --> 00:44:32,331
Use outside forms.

699
00:44:32,331 --> 00:44:34,849
Some teams do not use Angular Forms.

700
00:44:34,849 --> 00:44:37,726
Offering a checked model() as well is useful,

701
00:44:37,726 --> 00:44:41,683
but then forms and the model must write the same signal,

702
00:44:41,683 --> 00:44:45,640
and the documentation must say "use one or the other on

703
00:44:45,640 --> 00:44:46,719
a given instance".

704
00:44:46,719 --> 00:44:47,079
Validators.

705
00:44:47,079 --> 00:44:48,878
Validators.requiredTrue works without extra code.

706
00:44:48,878 --> 00:44:52,115
A component with built-in validation would also provide NG_VALIDATORS.

707
00:44:52,115 --> 00:44:55,352
Indeterminate state for "select all" checkboxes is a property

708
00:44:55,352 --> 00:44:58,590
(indeterminate), not an attribute, and needs its own input.

709
00:44:58,590 --> 00:45:00,388
Tests that use real forms.

710
00:45:00,388 --> 00:45:03,986
Each bug above is caught by a test that binds

711
00:45:03,986 --> 00:45:07,223
a real FormControl and calls reset(), patchValue() and disable().

712
00:45:07,223 --> 00:45:10,460
Testing the component in isolation would miss all four.

713
00:45:11,835 --> 00:45:14,245
API-004 · Follow-up 1

714
00:45:15,370 --> 00:45:19,344
Why does onChange during writeValue mark the control dirty?

715
00:45:19,344 --> 00:45:22,435
Which flag does the forms API set?

716
00:45:27,780 --> 00:45:32,028
Forms registers a view-to-model callback that marks the control pending dirty for

717
00:45:32,028 --> 00:45:36,277
a user change, then commits dirty state according to the update policy.

718
00:45:36,277 --> 00:45:41,234
Calling that callback during writeValue falsely takes the user-change path during a programmatic write.

719
00:45:41,234 --> 00:45:44,420
With updateOn blur, the pending state may commit later,

720
00:45:44,420 --> 00:45:47,607
so timing differs. writeValue should update only the view.

721
00:45:47,607 --> 00:45:52,564
Test reset leaves the form pristine and verify genuine user interaction marks it dirty.

722
00:45:53,939 --> 00:45:56,424
API-004 · Follow-up 2

723
00:45:57,550 --> 00:46:02,331
How would you build a ui-radio-group that works with formControlName on the group?

724
00:46:07,685 --> 00:46:12,421
Put the value accessor on the group so it represents one selected value.

725
00:46:12,421 --> 00:46:15,701
Individual radio items report user selection to the group,

726
00:46:15,701 --> 00:46:18,615
while the group handles writeValue, onChange, touched behavior,

727
00:46:18,615 --> 00:46:19,709
and disabled propagation.

728
00:46:19,709 --> 00:46:22,988
Use native radio semantics or a complete radiogroup keyboard

729
00:46:22,988 --> 00:46:26,267
pattern, unique grouping names, and an accessible group label.

730
00:46:26,267 --> 00:46:28,818
Object values may need a comparison contract.

731
00:46:28,818 --> 00:46:31,368
Programmatic writes must not emit user changes,

732
00:46:31,368 --> 00:46:35,012
and moving focus within the group should follow the chosen

733
00:46:35,012 --> 00:46:35,740
touched policy.

734
